# This repository stores every text file with LF, and three things depend on
# that: prettier is configured for LF (`lint:format` lists a CRLF file as
# different), `sh deploy.sh` runs on a Linux runner and a CRLF script fails on
# the carriage returns, and the committed openapi.json is compared byte for
# byte by CI.
#
# Git on this machine has `core.autocrlf=true` in its local config, which
# rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout -- so a plain `git checkout` of a
# file was enough to make `npm run lint` fail on it, with nothing in the diff
# to explain why. Pinning eol here fixes it for every clone without anyone
# having to change a git setting.
#
# After adding this, `git add --renormalize .` once brings an existing working
# tree into line.
* text=auto eol=lf
